# Retire policy 2026-11-20: still in production in 2026 with no announced end; retire dates commented out. Revisit when an end is announced.
# Lexus ES XZ10 four-door saloon, 2018 onwards.
#
# The seventh-generation ES: the front-wheel-drive executive saloon with the
# large spindle grille, the sharp headlamps and the long, low body. It is the
# first ES sold new in Britain (from January 2019); the earlier generations
# were not UK models and are not represented.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lexus_ES
#
# Dimensions 4.960-4.975 x 1.865 x 1.445-1.455 m, wheelbase 2.870 m.
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a true level side elevation of an ES 300h
# (AXZH10); the front and rear three-quarters are the same car.
#
# Colours: grade (a) for the three launch colours named in the Lexus UK
# release of 19 September 2018: Sonic White, Sonic Titanium and Azure Blue;
# grade (b) for Graphite Black from the later European palette. Weights 15,
# 13, 12, 10, total 50, provisional.
#
# Speed 180 km/h (electronically limited). Comfort 100/480, on the line
# 330 + 1.5 x 100: a quiet hybrid executive cabin. Class 2.
# Dates are road presence: 2019 intro, retire dates commented out (still in production in 2026).
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/lexus-es-xz10.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/lexus-es-xz10.dae. References:
# citycars/references/lexus-es-xz10/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the spindle grille is a straight-sided trapezoid rather
# than the curved spindle, its vertical bars and the tick-shaped DRL are not
# modelled, and the wheels are plain discs. The rear window and boot are slightly
# longer than the photographs. At 128 px the low beltline, large spindle grille
# and slim swept lamps read as an ES XZ10.


